Problems in Multithreading

Now comes the dangerous part.

Shared Memory Problem

Suppose:

Bank Balance = 1000

Two threads execute:

Withdraw 100
Withdraw 100

Simultaneously.

Thread 1 reads:

1000

Thread 2 reads:

1000

Thread 1 writes:

900

Thread 2 writes:

900

Expected:

800

Actual:

900

Wrong result.

This is called:

Race Condition
What Is Race Condition?

When multiple threads access shared data simultaneously and outcome depends on timing.

Example:

Thread A
Thread B

both updating same variable.

Result becomes unpredictable.

Real-Life Example

Imagine two cashiers updating the same account balance without coordination.

Errors occur.

Thread Safety

A program is thread-safe if multiple threads can execute correctly without corrupting data.

Solution to Race Conditions

OS provides:

Mutex
Semaphore
Monitor
Locks

We'll study these later.

